Torn Smart Seller – Item Market Helper

Hey everyone!

I’m not sure if something similar already exists, but I wanted to share a small userscript I made because it has been making Item Market listings much easier for me.

I tend to sell a lot of the same items, and I got tired of constantly deciding how many to sell, what to keep, and re-entering prices every time.

So I made Torn Smart Seller to remember those decisions and automatically prepare the Item Market listing page for me.

It does not submit listings automatically. It only prepares the quantities and prices, so you can still review everything before pressing Torn’s final Add to market button.

What does it do?

Every item can be assigned one of three rules:

Sell all
Automatically enters your entire available quantity.

Keep 1
Automatically sells everything except one copy.

Never sell
Leaves the item out of the sale.

Once you classify an item, Smart Seller remembers your choice locally.

The next time that item appears on the Add Listing page, the script already knows what to do with it.

Unclassified Items

When Smart Seller finds an item it has never seen before, it marks it as Unclassified.

The selector gets a small glow so new items are easy to notice.

You also don’t have to search through your entire inventory to find them.

If there are any unclassified items, Smart Seller automatically expands its panel and shows an Unclassified Items section containing:

Item icon

Item name

Available quantity

Category selector


You can classify them directly from the Smart Seller panel.

Once classified, they disappear from the Unclassified section automatically.

Automatic Pricing

Smart Seller can automatically calculate prices using Torn’s displayed RRP.

You simply choose a percentage adjustment.

For example:

5 → RRP + 5%
-5 → RRP - 5%
0 → exact RRP

So if an item has an RRP of $10,000 and your adjustment is set to 5, Smart Seller will enter:

$10,500

No Torn API key is required.

Fixed Prices

You can also assign a Fixed Price to individual items.

A fixed price always takes priority over the normal RRP percentage calculation.

For example, if you always want to sell a certain item for exactly $25,000, simply enter:

25000

Smart Seller will then always use that price for that item.

If you remove the fixed price and leave the field blank, the item goes back to using your normal RRP adjustment.

Fixed prices can be edited directly from the Item Market list.

Saved Items Manager

Clicking Saved at the top of the Smart Seller panel opens a larger management view.

This gives you an easy way to manage everything Smart Seller already knows.

It displays:

Name | Category | Fixed Price

There is also a search bar, which is especially useful once you have a lot of saved items.

From this screen you can directly change:

Sell all

Keep 1

Never sell

Fixed prices


So you don’t need to wait for an item to appear in your inventory just to edit its settings.

Auto-Prepare

By default, Smart Seller automatically prepares known items when you open the Add Listing page.

That means it fills in the appropriate quantity and price based on your saved settings.

If you prefer, you can disable Auto-prepare known items and use the Apply now button manually instead.

Import / Export

Everything is stored locally through Tampermonkey.

Smart Seller does not upload your item settings to an external server.

The panel includes Export All and Import All, allowing you to back up or move your configuration to another browser or computer.

The exported data includes things such as:

Item classifications

Fixed prices

RRP percentage adjustment

Auto-prepare setting

Smart Seller settings


Just export the JSON, save it somewhere, and import it on the other device.

Installation

Smart Seller is available on Greasy Fork.

You will need a userscript manager such as Tampermonkey installed in your browser.

Installation is simple:

1. Install Tampermonkey if you don’t already have it.


2. Open the Torn Smart Seller page on Greasy Fork.


3. Click Install this script.


4. Tampermonkey will open the userscript installation page.


5. Click Install.


6. Go to Torn → Item Market → Add Listing.



Smart Seller should appear automatically.

Installing it through Greasy Fork also makes updating to newer versions much easier through Tampermonkey.

How I use it

My workflow is basically:

The first time I see an item, I decide:

Sell everything?
Keep one?
Never sell it?

After that, I generally don’t need to think about that item again.

Whenever I open Add Listing, Smart Seller automatically fills in the quantities and prices I normally use.

I just review everything and submit the listing myself.

That was really the main reason I made it: less repetitive clicking and typing when selling inventory.

I don’t know if there is already another script doing something similar or even something better, but this one has been making my life easier, so I figured I might as well share it in case someone else finds it useful too.


